{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>From shortness of spirit.</b> Perhaps, since they were not sons of Torah, they did not listen; and therefore it is called <b>shortness of spirit</b>, for the Torah broadens a person's heart." "<b>And from harsh labor.</b> The reason it said <b>and from labor</b> — this tells that besides the pain of the labor, they additionally had shortness of spirit; and the reason is that when they saw how heavy the work was upon them, their spirit grew short aside from the specific pain of the labor. Also, it is the nature of a person whose spirit is short that he cannot work, for he grows weak from his pain. And the two are interrelated; therefore it said <b>and from labor</b> — for their spirit was short and their labor was also heavy." "<b>Further</b>, regarding the fact that Israel were informed with the tidings of the redemption, their hearts expanded and their souls and spirit revived; and when they returned to servitude — even though they were not enslaved except to the usual measure or less — nevertheless their spirit would grow short. One who understands the natural constitution of the human composition will understand the matter. And the verse further informs that they also heavy their yoke upon them beyond the usual, and that is its saying <b>and from labor</b> etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:25:06.420552971Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}